DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The echo service module for PAM displays its arguments to the user, sepa‐
     rated by spaces, using the current conversation function.

     If the %% character occurs anywhere in the arguments to ppaamm__eecchhoo, it is
     assumed to introduce one of the following escape sequences:

     %%HH    The name of the host on which the client runs (PAM_RHOST).

     %%ss    The current service name (PAM_SERVICE).

     %%tt    The name of the controlling tty (PAM_TTY).

     %%UU    The applicant's user name (PAM_RUSER).

     %%uu    The target account's user name (PAM_USER).

     Any other two-character sequence beginning with %% expands to the charac‐
     ter following the %% character.

